the Prime Minister and health secretary  have addressed the current NHS crisis  Steve Barkley says Hospital capacity  problems have been caused by patients  who do not need to be there but where  else are these pressures coming from  here you can see all 19 regions where  NHS trusts have declared critical  incidents in England during the last  week this is not normal even during a  very busy winter it shows what pressure  the NHS is under the biggest issue what  is driving this pressure is the lack of  social care for patients who are  medically fit to be discharged  there are over 12 000 people in hospital  that don't need to be there but can't be  discharged safely into the community  people are being urged to call 111  unless it's a real emergency in the week  before Christmas six hundred thousand  people call the service that's up over  two-thirds on the same period last year  and almost a third of callers abandoned  their calls before they were answered  and for patients trying to see their GP  there are also big delays despite  pledges by the government for 6 000 new  GPS by 2024 the number of fully trained  GPS has fallen by almost 2 000.  healthy to say these pressures are  driving up excess deaths not counting  the number of people who've died from  covid over the last six months there  have been an average of 800 extra debts  per week compared to the five-year  average in England and Wales Health  analysts say this is largely down to  delays in the NHS but NHS leaders and  the government dispute this  it's impossible to work out precisely  what makes up those 800 excess deaths  and there are many possible factors in  particular the consequences of the  pandemic the delayed treatment what you  might call you know the chronic delayed  care that people are you know have been  receiving it's quite plausible that  hundreds of those cases  um you know an estimate has been made  between three and five hundred and I I  think it's quite plausible that of that  sort of order of magnitude could be  attributable to the delays in people  getting into Hospital  the warnings of a triple democovid flu  and emergency department pressures have  been sounded for some time Health  leaders said this could be the worst  winter in the nhs's history and it looks  like those warnings might be coming true
 

